From d75eb0493fbbabba8abc1e767cd00ac32aebc325 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Struan Bartlett <struan.bartlett@NewsNow.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:22:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] passthrough: Let the guest cache symbolic link targets

Negotiate FUSE_CACHE_SYMLINKS unless --cache=never is in effect.
Without it, the guest kernel sends a FUSE_READLINK request every time
a path walk passes through a symbolic link, even with --cache=always,
because FUSE caches link targets in the page cache only when the
server opts in.

This is common on distributions built on BusyBox, where /bin/true,
/bin/sh, /bin/ls and so on are all symbolic links to /bin/busybox:
every exec() of one of them costs a READLINK round trip, as does
every lstat()-and-readlink() pair from `ls -l`.

Caching is safe: a symbolic link's target cannot be changed in place;
replacing it creates a new inode, which the guest sees through the
usual entry and attribute revalidation for the cache mode in use.
virtiofsd holds an O_PATH descriptor (or file handle) for every inode
the guest knows, so the host cannot reuse the inode number for a new
link while the guest still has the old target cached.

With --cache=never the behaviour is unchanged, so that mode still
caches nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/passthrough/mod.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/passthrough/mod.rs b/src/passthrough/mod.rs
index 38f49db..d0712d3 100644
--- a/src/passthrough/mod.rs
+++ b/src/passthrough/mod.rs
@@ -1520,6 +1520,16 @@ impl FileSystem for PassthroughFs {
         } else {
             FsOptions::empty()
         };
+        // A symbolic link's target cannot change without the link being replaced by a new
+        // inode, and we hold a reference to every inode the guest knows about, so the host
+        // cannot reuse it either.  So unless the guest is told not to cache anything, let it
+        // keep link targets in its page cache instead of sending READLINK on every path walk
+        // through a symbolic link.
+        if !matches!(self.cfg.cache_policy, CachePolicy::Never)
+            && capable.contains(FsOptions::CACHE_SYMLINKS)
+        {
+            opts |= FsOptions::CACHE_SYMLINKS;
+        }
         if self.cfg.writeback && capable.contains(FsOptions::WRITEBACK_CACHE) {
             opts |= FsOptions::WRITEBACK_CACHE;
             self.writeback.store(true, Ordering::Relaxed);
-- 
